===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|caterwrawen}}, from {{m|enm|cater||cat}} + {{m|enm|wrawen}}, {{m|enm|wrawlen||cry like a cat}}, equivalent to {{compound|en|cat|waul}}. Compare {{cog|nds|katerwaulen|t=to cry like a cat}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|ca|ter|waul|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈkæt.ə.wɔːl/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈkæt.ɚ.wɔl/|/ˈkæt.ɚ.wɑl/|lang=en}}
* {{a|cot-caught|northern cities vowel shift}} {{IPA|/ˈkæt.ɚ.wɑl/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-caterwaul.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

